Definitive answer on the regex question — found it in the dependency:

```js
// node_modules/@mariozechner/pi-ai/dist/providers/openai-completions.js
317:  output.errorMessage = error instanceof Error ? error.message : JSON.stringify(error);
304:  throw new Error(output.errorMessage || "Provider returned an error stop reason");
```

`pi-ai` reduces the provider error to `error.message` and rethrows a bare `Error`. The HTTP status, OpenAI's `error.code: "insufficient_quota"`, `error.type` — all discarded inside the dependency before our code sees it. That's why the prod log showed `{"name":"Error","message":"You have no credits remaining…"}` and nothing else.

So we're not choosing prose over status codes; the runtime throws the structured error away. Verifying the fix is green, then I'll lay out the real fix:

