content.text:
Reverted clean — nothing from that approach is left.

You're right, and here's the concrete version of it. The proxy already has everything:

```ts
// secret-proxy.ts:1030 — expectedOrganizationId and resolvedSlug are in scope
const response = await fetch(upstream, { method, headers, body });
if (!response.ok) {
  logger.warn(`Upstream returned ${response.status} …`);   // ← status, then discarded
}
```

`429` / `401` / `403` / `402` is the classification. `Retry-After` is the horizon, as a number. No prose, no year-less date to guess, no dependency on `pi-ai` preserving anything. It's our code, it sees every provider call for every org, and it already knows which org and which provider.

That supersedes the mark half of #2525 (which routes health the long way round through the worker) and removes the parser from the park decision entirely. The one thing it doesn't cover is the *user-facing text* — `classifyError` still drives which CTA renders in chat — but the proxy can inject a structured code into the error body so that stops being a guessing game too.

This changes something I shipped two hours ago and touches the credential proxy, so I want your call before I build it rather than after.

